I know you didn't write all this, but while you're rewriting anyway, I suggest simplifying this logic as such:

```c++
const char *l_cname = l._data ? l._data->cname : nullptr;
const char *r_cname = r._data ? r._data->cname : nullptr;

if (!r_cname) {
	return false;
}
if (!l_cname) {
	return true;
}
return str_compare(l_cname, r_cname) < 0;
```

And analogously for the other combinations. I think it makes the edge cases clearer, and should be minimally faster too.

